ogeneous power instance.","effect_on_target":"Realizes x².","status":"understood"},{"id":"D041","name":"instOfNatAtLeastTwo","meaning":"Numerals at least two via NatCast.","effect_on_target":"Interprets real 2.","status":"understood"},{"id":"D042","name":"instOfNatNat","meaning":"Canonical Nat numeral instance.","effect_on_target":"Supplies natural literals.","status":"understood"},{"id":"D043","name":"instOneNNReal","meaning":"One on NNReal.","effect_on_target":"Supplies Gaussian parameter 1.","status":"understood"},{"id":"D044","name":"ProbabilityTheory.gaussianReal","meaning":"Dirac at μ if v=0; otherwise volume with gaussianPDF μ v.","effect_on_target":"At 0,1 defines the measure in the first equality.","status":"understood"}],"translation":{"binders":[],"hypotheses":[],"conclusions":["LocalDef001 = Real.measureSpace.volume.withDensity (gaussianPDF 0 1).","gaussianPDFReal 0 1 = fun x ↦ (1/sqrt(2π))*exp(-x²/2)."],"mathematical_definitions":["LocalDef001 = LocalDef002 = gaussianReal 0 1.","gaussianReal μ v is Dirac μ when v=0 and otherwise volume.withDensity (gaussianPDF μ v).","gaussianPDF μ v x = ENNReal.ofReal (gaussianPDFReal μ v x).","gaussianPDFReal μ v x = exp(-(x-μ)²/(2v))/sqrt(2πv)."],"proposition_plain_english":"The Gaussian measure at 0 and 1 is real volume weighted by its Gaussian density, whose real formula is exp(-x²/2)/sqrt(2π)."},"restrictions_and_vacuity_risks":["No hypotheses: not vacuous by implication.","Only parameters 0 and 1 are covered.","Equalities are exact, including function equality, not merely almost everywhere.","No separate normalization, measurability, or integrability claim.","The measure conjunct uses ENNReal gaussianPDF; the formula conjunct uses gaussianPDFReal."],"ambiguities":["Real.measureSpace is exposed only as inferInstance, so its concrete volume construction is hidden.","Local names are opaque, but their supplied bodies identify gaussianReal 0 1.","The packet gives v's algebraic role but no prose label."]}
